i","town":"Varanasi","latitude":25.26603,"longitude":82.98785,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Assi River","river_distance_km":1.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Varanasi near Banaras Hindu University, also called the New Vishwanath or Birla Temple. Visitors come to pray for family wellbeing, and it draws many students. It is said to have the world's tallest temple tower, with a spire about 250 feet high. The university administers it directly.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Lal Bahadur Shastri International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":24.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Banaras (Manduadih) railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Vishwanath Mandir), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"461df3b1-ed49-4360-9ceb-223bdb5bffcf","name":"Masroor Rock-cut Temples, Kangra","deity":"Shiva (a linga stands in the sanctum), in a multi-shrine complex; Vishnu, Devi and Surya associations are also noted","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Kangra","town":"Masrur","latitude":32.0726,"longitude":76.1371,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Beas","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T21:24:56.957301+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"The complex was first reported by Henry Shuttleworth in 1913 and surveyed by Harold Hargreaves of the ASI in 1915, who corrected the earlier description of it as a Vaishnava temple by noting the Shiva linga. Michael Meister dates it to the first half of the 8th century. It was never completed and was damaged by earthquake. A local attribution to the Pandavas is common but was not sourced.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Gaggal Airport, Kangra","nearest_airport_distance_km":35.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nagrota Suriyan railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Masrur Temples); Kangra district site","architecture_style":"Monolithic rock-cut Nagara-style shikhara temples on a square mandala plan, with a sacred pool. An ASI-protected monument","construction_century":8},{"id":"463e74a7-e759-4ecd-8e87-4b46fabecf99","name":"Tiruvelukkai Temple","deity":"Vishnu as Azhagiya Singar (Narasimha)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Kanchipuram","town":"Kanchipuram","latitude":12.82222,"longitude":79.70667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vegavathi River","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:14.599574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Divya Desam in Kanchipuram praised in the Nalayira Divya Prabandham, where Vishnu is worshipped as Azhagiya Singar with Lakshmi as Amruthavalli. Believed to date from the late Pallava period, it has later Chola and Vijayanagara contributions, three inscriptions, a granite wall and a three-tiered gateway tower.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":53.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kanchipuram East railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Tiruvelukkai), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":8},{"id":"464a311d-ecd0-48e7-ba19-c4bd92f618a3","name":"Sri Venkateswara Swamy Temple, Tirumala","deity":"Venkateswara (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Tirupati","town":"Tirumala","latitude":13.6833,"longitude":79.3475,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"Dedicated Sandhya Vandanam hall near Vishnu Nivasam guest houses; water taps available all day.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"partial","samidhadhanam_notes":"Open spaces near the choultries can be used; check with TTD staff for a quiet spot during peak hours.","food_tier":"brahmin_run_kitchen","food_source_name":"TTD Annadanam & Vishnu Nivasam Brahmin Bhojanam","food_source_contact":"+91-877-227-7777","food_distance_km":0.5,"nearest_river_name":"Kalyani Dam","river_distance_km":3,"best_season_notes":"Sept–Feb is cooler and less crowded; avoid Brahmotsavam week unless attending.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T19:02:16.315601+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds that Venkateswara took residence on the Seven Hills at the close of the Dvapara yuga, and that he borrowed from Kubera to meet the expenses of his marriage to Padmavati. Pilgrims' offerings in the hundi are understood as helping repay that debt, which is why the deity is also called Venkataramana, the lord of the hill.","etiquette_notes":"Modest dress is expected (shoulders and knees covered); shorts and sleeveless tops are usually turned away at the sanctum. Devotees often shave their heads here as an offering — entirely optional, with dedicated tonsure halls on site if you choose to.","native_name":"శ్రీ వేంకటేశ్వర స్వామి ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":"03:00:00","morning_closes_at":"22:00:00","evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Effectively open the better part of the day via a token-based queue system rather than fixed darshan sessions; token counters have their own hours that change seasonally.","accessibility_notes":"The queue complex uses a mix of ramps and steps; token-holders can expect a long walk (sometimes hours) through the queue lines before reaching the sanctum. Ask staff about assistance for elderly or mobility-impaired pilgrims — dedicated slower-moving lines exist.","nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tirupati Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":22,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Dravidian, developed over many centuries under Pallava, Chola, and Vijayanagara patronage","construction_century":null},{"id":"46c63ef1-85c0-4f14-8fa2-b94da2faf177","name":"Balasubramanya Swamy Temple, Teynampet","deity":"Balasubramanya (Murugan)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Teynampet","latitude":13.043,"longitude":80.249,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":"Jan–Feb for Thaipusam; otherwise Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Reported to be about 500 years old, a Murugan shrine in Teynampet that predates the neighbourhood's modern commercial development.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":10.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mandaveli railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"476d077a-4be3-4792-a6d8-28bb9204f7ba","name":"Lakshmi Narasimha Navaneetha Krishnan Temple, Nanganallur","deity":"Lakshmi Narasimha and Navaneetha Krishna (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Nanganallur","latitude":12.9775,"longitude":80.1935,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":3.2,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in 1974,