ude":15.941,"longitude":77.533,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The Tungabhadra runs alongside the matha, with steps down to the water.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Matha Anna Prasadam — free meals to several thousand daily, a practice said to date back to Raghavendra Swamy himself (paused on Ekadasi and eclipse days)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.1,"nearest_river_name":"Tungabhadra","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb. The Aradhana Mahotsava (Jul/Aug) draws very large crowds.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:44:40.752775+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"The brindavana of Sri Raghavendra Tirtha, the seventeenth-century Madhwa saint and Dvaita scholar, who by tradition entered live samadhi here in 1671. The matha remains one of the principal centres of the Madhwa sampradaya.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"శ్రీ రాఘవేంద్ర స్వామి మఠం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":72.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mantralayam Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":25.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"48275ff6-1c87-423b-b56e-729b6f01aef6","name":"Khole Ke Hanuman Ji Temple","deity":"Hanuman","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Jaipur","town":"Jaipur","latitude":26.9401,"longitude":75.8548,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Amanisha River","river_distance_km":5.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:10:09.085477+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Hanuman temple about 9 km from the centre of Jaipur. Besides worshippers, domestic and foreign tourists come to enjoy the scenic natural setting of the place. The article names Hanuman as a major Hindu deity, and the site lies in Rajasthan, India, within the Jaipur district.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":12.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Jaipur Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Khole Ke Hanuman Ji Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"48623915-b486-4f60-aa1b-15104f8190bd","name":"Jogulamba Temple, Alampur","deity":"Jogulamba (Devi)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Jogulamba Gadwal","town":"Alampur","latitude":15.8833,"longitude":78.1167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Tungabhadra","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:30:52.99453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Set beside the Navabrahma group of ninth-century Shiva temples near the Tungabhadra-Krishna confluence, and counted as the fifth of the 18 Maha Shakti Peethas — tradition holds Sati's upper teeth fell here. The original temple dates to the 6th century CE under the Badami Chalukyas. Jogulamba is depicted seated on a corpse with a scorpion, frog and lizard on her head, and is held to grant siddhi (spiritual attainment) in yoga.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"జోగులాంబ ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":19.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Alampur Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":6},{"id":"48a9147b-3adf-4432-9d2e-e02bc19d0c30","name":"Daksheswar Mahadev Temple","deity":"Shiva as Daksheswar Mahadev","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Haridwar","town":"Haridwar","latitude":29.92187,"longitude":78.14584,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganges River","river_distance_km":1.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Located in Kankhal, about 4 km from Haridwar, and named for King Daksha Prajapati, the father of Sati. Queen Dhankaur built the present temple in 1810 and it was rebuilt in 1962. Shaiva devotees make a pilgrimage here on Maha Shivaratri.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":30.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Jwalapur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Daksheswar Mahadev Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":19},{"id":"48d00157-632d-4d81-8b36-5a37c0257922","name":"Shri Shri Hari Baladev Jew Bije, Baripada","deity":"Vishnu as Jagannath","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Mayurbhanj","town":"Baripada","latitude":21.92916,"longitude":86.72331,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Budhabalanga River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Jagannath temple in Baripada, Mayurbhanj, known as the second Sreekhetra after Puri. It is a Rekha-style temple built in 1575 CE by Baidyanath Bhanj, on the same principles as the Kakharua Baidyanath temple. Its Rath Yatra is notable for giving women devotees priority in pulling Subhadra's chariot.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jamshedpur Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":113.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhanjpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Shri Hari Baladev Jew Bije, Baripada), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Rekha (Orissan)","construction_century":16},{"id":"490eba12-4348-437f-9360-0508f50ff1da","name":"Mahavir Mandir, Patna","deity":"Hanuman, worshipped as Sankat Mochan — unusually, two Hanuman idols share the sanctum, one in a blessing pose and one in meditation","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Patna","town":"Patna","latitude":25.60389,"longitude":85.13639,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganges River","river_distance_km":3.4,"best_season_notes":"Ram Navami (queues reportedly exceeding 1km) and Hanuman Jayanti are the major festivals; Tuesdays and Saturdays are the traditional heavy-worship days for Hanuman.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:21:41.744062+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A 1948 Patna High Court ruling recorded that the temple \"has existed since time immemorial,\" but its documented modern establishment traces to the Ramanandi ascetic Swami Balanand, around 1730 CE — the \"time immemorial\" framing is tradition, not verified history. It rose to prominence after 1947 as Partition refugees settled in Patna, and courts declared it a public temple in 1948. The old structure was demolished; the current marble temple, run since by the Shri Mahavir Sthan Nyas Samiti trust under Acharya Kishore Kunal, was completed in 1987. The trust reportedly has the second-highest temple-trust budget in North India after Vaishno Devi, and funds hospitals including the Mahavir Cancer Institute.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Per third-party temple-info sources, not the trust's own official statement: open roughly 5am–10pm daily, with morning darshan 5am–1pm, a midday closure, and evening darshan 3–10pm. Mangala Aarti around 5am, evening Aarti roughly 7:30–8pm (varies seasonally).","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jay Prakash Narayan International Airport, Patna","nearest_airport_distance_km":6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Patna Junction","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"1948 Patna High Court ruling; Shri Mahavir Sthan Nyas Samiti records","architecture_style":"Nagara style, marble construction, roughly 57m (187ft) tall","construction_century":20},{"id":"49db9001-52e1-4b43-b66d-87fe612005ef","name":"Mangeshi Temple, Priol","deity":"Manguesh (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Goa","district":"Ponda","town":"Priol","latitude":15.4256,"longitude":73.9622,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cumbarjua Canal River","river_distance_km":2.3,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb, cool and dry season away from Goa's monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of Goa's largest and most visited Shiva temples, also relocated to its present site from Old Goa (Kushasthali) during the Portuguese period to escape the demolition of Hindu shrines there.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"मंगेशी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Goa International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Karmali railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"49e885d4-442e-40c2-a702-b6e4fa392a57","name":"Bhavishya Badri Temple","deity":"Vishnu (Bhavishya Badri)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Panch Badri"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Subain","latitude":30.53,"longitude":79.7,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dhauli Ganga River","river_distance_km":3.5,"best_season_notes":"Reached via a roughly 3 km trail from the motor road beyond Tapovan, up the Dhauliganga valley; a warm-season visit (May–Oct) is most practical.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T08:35:20.91066+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the five Panch Badri shrines, known as the \"Future Badri\" — tradition holds that when the path to Badrinath eventually becomes impassable, this temple will become the seat of Vishnu's worship in its place.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"भविष्य बद्री मंदिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":150.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"4a191d80-55fd-43aa-ab53-e26aa1343084","name":"Vadapalani Murugan Temple","deity":"Murugan (Andavar)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Vadapalani","latitude":13.0503,"longitude":80.2121,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":2.6,"best_season_notes":"Jan–Feb for Thaipusam and Panguni Uthiram; otherwise Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Reported to be around 125 years old, making it one of the newer major temples on this list — yet it has grown into one of Chennai's most visited Murugan shrines, drawing huge crowds especially on Karthigai and Panguni Uthiram.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kodambakkam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"4a1a44d8-279e-413e-8096-8adb98696e0b","name":"Lakshmi Devi Temple, Doddagaddavalli","deity":"Mahalakshmi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Hassan","town":"Doddagaddavalli","latitude":13.096,"longitude":76.00389,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Yagachi River","river_distance_km":6.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:14.599574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An early 12th-century temple regarded as the first Hoysala temple, with four shrines around a shared mandapa: Mahalakshmi to the east, Kali north, Shiva west, and a now-empty Vishnu shrine south. A separate Bhairava shrine and smaller shrines stand in the compound, with Nagara-style towers.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shivamogga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":94.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Alur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":12.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Lakshmi Devi Temple, Doddagaddavalli), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Hoysala; Nagara shikharas","construction_century":12},{"id":"4a26c625-9b05-4dc5-ac4b-212ebaff79f5","name":"Srikanteshwara Temple, Nanjangud","deity":"Srikanteshwara / Nanjundeshwara (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Mysuru","town":"Nanjangud","latitude":12.1167,"longitude":76.6833,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kapila (Kabini)","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar for Maha Shivaratri; otherwise Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T17:30:52.99453+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Known as the \"Dakshina Kashi\" (Kashi of the South) for the sanctity of bathing in the Kapila river here. Tradition holds sage Gautama first installed a linga at the site; the temple grew from a small 9th-century Ganga-era shrine to its present scale under Vijayanagara patronage. The deity's names, Nanjunda and Srikanteshwara, both refer to Shiva's swallowing of the halahala poison during the churning of the ocean. A well-known 18th-century episode holds Tipu Sultan's blinded elephant regained its sight after 48 days of temple rituals, after which he donated an emerald linga still preserved here.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಶ್ರೀಕಂಠೇಶ್ವರ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mysore Mandakalli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":13.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nanjangud Town railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"4a72f871-7175-423d-ba12-00c306d75eb7","name":"Hangseshwari Temple","deity":"Hangseswari (Dakshina Kali)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Hooghly","town":"Bansberia","latitude":22.96432,"longitude":88.39981,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Saraswati River","river_distance_km":1.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:53.924452+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple at Bansberia in Hooghly, West Bengal, to Hangseswari, worshipped as a form of Kali. Its foundation was laid in 1799 by Raja Nrisinhadeb Roy and it was finished by his widow Rani Sankari in 1814. It is noted for 13 lotus-bud shaped towers in the ratna style.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":34.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bansh Baria railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Hangseshwari Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Ratna (13 towers)","construction_century":19},{"id":"4a8aa7be-3413-4344-b5e7-74432ddc0acf","name":"Surya Temple, Ranchi","deity":"Surya","sampradaya":"Saura","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jharkhand","district":"Ranchi","town":"Lotang","latitude":23.18167,"longitude":85.56167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Raisa Nadi River","river_distance_km":6.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A hilltop sun temple complex near Bundu on the Ranchi-Tata road, built in the form of a large chariot with eighteen wheels and seven horses. Shiva, Parvati and Ganesha are also enshrined. A charitable trust built it, with the foundation stone laid in 1991 and consecration in 1994. A pond is used for bathing during Chhath Puja.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":28.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Gautamdhara railway station","nearest_railway_dist