te":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Park Town","latitude":13.095,"longitude":80.284,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cooum","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Jan–Feb for Thaipusam; otherwise Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Reported to be over 1,000 years old, one of the older surviving temples in what is now Chennai's Park Town district, predating most of the area's colonial-era development.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":17,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Washermanpet railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"4aca626c-9e6b-44d2-b316-ec648cc630d3","name":"Padmanabhaswamy Temple, Thiruvananthapuram","deity":"Vishnu (Padmanabha)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Malai Nadu Divya Desam"],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Thiruvananthapuram","town":"Thiruvananthapuram","latitude":8.4828,"longitude":76.9439,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple Ootupura (dining hall) near the north gate — free annadanam around midday","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.1,"nearest_river_name":"Killi River","river_distance_km":1.5,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb; note the temple's traditional dress code is strictly enforced.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Vishnu reclines here on Ananta, the serpent, in the yoga-nidra posture, visible through three doors — the head, the torso and the feet. The temple's traditional accounts connect its establishment with the sage Divakara Muni.","etiquette_notes":"Traditional dress code enforced: men wear a mundu/dhoti without a shirt; women wear a saree, or a long skirt (pavada) with a blouse for young girls. Photography is not permitted inside the sanctum precincts.","native_name":"ശ്രീ പദ്മനാഭസ്വാമി ക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":"04:30:00","morning_closes_at":"12:00:00","evening_opens_at":"17:00:00","evening_closes_at":"19:30:00","timings_notes":"Strict dress code checked at entry — see the etiquette notes above before you plan around these hours.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Thiruvananthapuram International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thiruvananthapuram Central","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Kerala","construction_century":18},{"id":"4ad62c07-daa8-438f-87d4-9847959b55de","name":"Subramaniya Swamy Temple, Thiruparankundram","deity":"Murugan as Subramaniya Swamy","sampradaya":"Kaumara","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Madurai","town":"Thirupparankundram","latitude":9.8798,"longitude":78.0711,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vaigai River","river_distance_km":7.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A rock-cut Murugan temple built into a hillock at Thiruparankundram, Madurai, and one of the Six Abodes of Murugan. The Pandyas built the original in the 6th century. Tradition holds that Murugan married Deivanai here and worshipped Shiva as Parangirinathar. The Kantha Sashti festival in Aipasi is the most prominent, and six daily rituals are followed.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":5.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruparankundram railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Subramaniya Swamy Temple, Thiruparankundram), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Rock-cut","construction_century":6},{"id":"4af2d9e4-f61d-4bc3-b8f9-f2463ca13900","name":"Maha Ganapathi Mahammaya Temple","deity":"Ganesha as Mahaganapati and Mahamaya (Shantadurga)","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Uttara Kannada","town":"Shirali","latitude":14.0317,"longitude":74.5233,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Venkatapura River","river_distance_km":0.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:38.196668+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple at Shirali in Uttara Kannada, dedicated to Ganesha as Mahaganapati together with the goddess Mahamaya, also called Shantadurga. It is the family temple of many Goud Saraswat Brahmin families, including Kamath, Bhat and Nayak lines. It is said to be about 400 years old and was renovated in 1904.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shivamogga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":119.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhatkal railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Maha Ganapathi Mahammaya Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"4b90d788-c137-4d24-9ecc-fe9760216296","name":"Karaneeswarar Temple, Mylapore","deity":"Karaneeswarar (Shiva) / Porkodi Amman","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Saptha Sthana Mylapore"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Chennai","town":"Mylapore, Chennai","latitude":13.035,"longitude":80.268,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Adyar River","river_distance_km":2.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T20:12:07.478318+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the Saptha Sthana Sthalangal, seven Shiva shrines in and around Mylapore traditionally said to have been worshipped by the Saptarishis (seven sages). Karaneeswarar's name means \"the Lord who is the cause,\" with Parvati worshipped here as Porkodi Amman. The temple may date to around the 12th century, though this is not firmly documented.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"கரணீஸ்வரர் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":11.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thirumayilai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition (Saptha Sthana)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":12},{"id":"4c52b6df-94cb-4dbc-9450-cf9ceb0cb776","name":"Sammakka Saralamma Temple, Medaram","deity":"Sammakka and Saralamma (tribal goddesses, worshipped as forms of Adi Parashakti)","sampradaya":null,"significance":["Tribal jatara"],"country":"India","state":"Telangana","district":"Mulugu","town":"Medaram","latitude":18.24194,"longitude":80.08528,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"The Jatara is held in the Telugu month of Magha (Jan–Feb), on even-numbered years, over four days.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:36:33.433509+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Not a built stone temple but an open-air site: Sammakka and her daughter Saralamma are marked by \"gaddelu\" (shrine platforms), traditionally under trees in the forest. Koya tribal legend holds that Sammakka was found as an infant glowing amid tigers and adopted, later marrying the Koya chieftain Pagididda Raju; in the 13th century, when the Kakatiya ruler Prataparudra moved against the tribal territory, her daughter Saralamma and others died in battle, and a warrior named Jampanna gave his life in the stream since renamed Jampanna Vagu in his memory. Sammakka herself is said to have vanished into the Chilakala Gutta hills rather than die, worshipped since in the form of vermilion (kumkuma bharani) found at that spot. This is oral Koya tradition, not epigraphically documented history. The Jatara held here is one of the largest tribal religious gatherings in the world.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Warangal Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":62.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chintalpalli railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":54.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Koya oral tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"4c64f417-90e1-4ad5-9f5f-2c8c253b6852","name":"Deva Mai Temple","deity":"Divine Mother (Deva Mai)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":"Reasi","town":"Katra","latitude":32.972,"longitude":74.8949,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chenab River","river_distance_km":7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:36.086063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Deva Mai is a temple to the Divine Mother about 4 km outside Katra in Reasi district, Jammu and Kashmir. It stands in the Siwalik Hills and is reached by a 3.5 km detour from the Jammu-Katra highway.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jammu Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":31.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shri M