","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dakshina Pinakini River","river_distance_km":3.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:14.599574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Dravidian-style temple near Bengaluru called Small Tirupati, resembling the Tirupati Venkateswara temple. Vishnu is worshipped as Venkateshwara with Lakshmi as Alamelumangamma. The main Brahmotsava falls in Shravana, with a chariot procession. A Sabha Administration Board manages it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Open 6:30 am to 7:30 pm daily.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kempegowda International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":37.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Devangonthi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":10.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Chikka Tirupati), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"50275554-efa0-4fa9-89ec-5483e39a6cf9","name":"Janaki Temple, Sitamarhi","deity":"Sita (Janaki), traditionally revered at the site as her birthplace","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Sitamarhi","town":"Sitamarhi","latitude":26.5865,"longitude":85.4668,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bagmati River","river_distance_km":13.1,"best_season_notes":"Janaki Navami, Vivaha Panchami and Ram Navami are the major festivals.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:21:41.744062+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Sitamarhi genuinely has two separate sites associated with Sita's birth, and this entry doesn't try to erase that. Janaki Sthan, in Sitamarhi town itself, is the older and better-documented site: land was endowed here in 1599 CE by King Narpati Singh of the Darbhanga Raj, with the first Mahant, Hiraram Das of Revasa Math, and a recorded 1923 Patna High Court succession case. Punaura Dham, a few kilometres away, is the more commonly cited site in popular/tourism tradition — per the Valmiki Ramayana, King Janaka found an infant girl in a furrow (sita) while ploughing near sage Pundrik's ashram during a famine-year yajna, giving her the names Sita and Janaki; this is scriptural legend, not archaeological history. A large new temple complex, the Janaki Janmasthali Mandir, is under construction at Punaura Dham (foundation stones laid December 2023 and August 2025, built by the Mahavir Mandir Trust) and is not yet operational — visitors today see the existing, smaller shrines at both sites, not the finished complex.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Muzzafarpur Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":54.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sitamarhi Junction","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Darbhanga Raj and Patna High Court records (Janaki Sthan); Valmiki Ramayana (Punaura Dham legend); Mahavir Mandir Trust project records","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"5099d26e-055f-491b-8ce5-1f4741437584","name":"Mamal Temple","deity":"Shiva as Mamaleshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":"Anantnag","town":"Pahalgam","latitude":34.00977,"longitude