,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:54:32.209521+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Maha Vishnu temple on the slope of Brahmagiri hill in north Wayanad, near the Karnataka border, at about 900 m altitude and 32 km from Mananthavady. It is counted among the 108 Abhimana Kshetrams of the Vaishnava tradition.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kannur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":49.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Mahé railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":54.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Thirunelli Temple)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"519e8572-48a9-41fe-9a20-e4db2ec1deee","name":"Bhakthavatsala Perumal Temple, Thirunindravur","deity":"Bhakthavatsala Perumal (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvallur","town":"Thirunindravur","latitude":13.1078,"longitude":80.0478,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Cooum River","river_distance_km":0.9,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the 108 Divya Desams, initially built by the Pallavas in the late 8th century, standing near the Hridayaleeswarar Shiva temple in Thirunindravur.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":18.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruninravur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey; Nalayira Divya Prabandham; historical record","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":8},{"id":"51c61931-26e1-476e-9d00-f53afa8807d1","name":"Durga Temple, Aihole","deity":"Originally Surya; now named for Durga","sampradaya":"Saura","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Bagalkot","town":"Aihole","latitude":16.02067,"longitude":75.88194,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Malaprabha River","river_distance_km":0.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T09:54:32.209521+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An early 8th-century temple, originally dedicated to Surya. It is called Durga because a durg (fortified lookout) was built on top of it after the 13th century, during the wars between Hindu kingdoms and the Sultanates; that structure has since been removed and the temple restored. It has the largest and most embellished relief panels in Aihole, depicting Shaiva, Vaishnava, Shakta and Vedic themes, and is a rare apsidal-plan example among early Chalukya temples. It is part of a pending UNESCO World Heritage nomination.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Hubballi Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":113.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Guledgudda Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":20.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Durga temple, Aihole)","architecture_style":"Early Chalukya; apsidal plan","construction_century":8},{"id":"51cb1ef7-ae19-4ba2-a532-b089b42335c2","name":"Omkareshwar Jyotirlinga","deity":"Shiva (Omkareshwar)","sampradaya":null,"significance":["Jyotirlinga"],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Khandwa","town":"Omkareshwar","latitude":22.2413,"longitude":76.1494,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"The temple sits on Mandhata island in the Narmada itself — river access is immediate.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Shri Omkar Prasadalay near Jhula Pul — meals at a nominal charge rather than fully free","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.3,"nearest_river_name":"Narmada","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar; footbridge access can flood in peak monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-04T18:03:34.795958+00:00","sthala_purana":"The island in the Narmada is held to be shaped like the syllable Om, from which the kshetra takes its name. The sthala purana relates that Shiva appeared here at the prayer of the Vindhya mountain, and that the lingam divided into two — Omkareshwar and Mamleshwar.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ओंकारेश्वर ज्योतिर्लिंग","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Devi Ahilya Bai Holkar Airport, Indore","nearest_airport_distance_km":80,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Omkareshwar Road Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":12,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Shiva Purana / Skanda Purana (Jyotirlinga tradition)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"51dd4de3-2420-4822-b73d-420e58a84061","name":"Bahucharaji Temple","deity":"Bahuchara Mata","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Mehsana","town":"Bahucharaji","latitude":23.5333,"longitude":72.1667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Saraswati","river_distance_km":5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar; a modest Shakti Peetha temple in the same Bhadarvi Purnima mela orbit as Ambaji — most comfortable outside Gujarat's hot, humid monsoon (Jun–Sep).","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Dedicated to Bahuchara Devi, whose vahana is a rooster. Tradition recounts several origin legends, including one where the goddess took her own life to escape bandits and cursed the land, later manifesting to bless a prince with a son on condition of dedicating his life to her service in feminine dress. The temple has long been a principal centre of devotion for Gujarat's Hijra (transgender) community, who traditionally regard Bahuchara Devi as their patron goddess.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"બહુચરાજી માતાનું મંદિર","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":69.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Rantej railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Devi Bhagavata Purana / Shakti Peetha tradition (Sati-limb legend)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"52