marked each year on Phulera Dooj. The premises include a shrine showing Krishna applying sindoor to Radha, the sacred well Venu Kup, and a Balarama temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Noida International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":58.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vrindavan railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Radha Krishna Vivah Sthali, Bhandirvan), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"528ae949-efd9-415b-8b55-6d3a219e80a0","name":"Tripurantaka Temple","deity":"Shiva as Tripurantakeshwara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Shimoga","town":"Belagavi","latitude":14.39389,"longitude":75.24389,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Western Chalukya temple built around 1070 CE at Balligavi in Shivamogga district, now in a poor state of repair. Its outer walls carry miniature erotic friezes, described as rare in Chalukyan art. Balligavi was once a learning centre for several faiths, and over 80 medieval inscriptions have been found there.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shivamogga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":72.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sagar Jambagaru railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":34.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Tripurantaka Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Western Chalukya","construction_century":11},{"id":"52f27845-ce73-45f8-90df-0c22c5bc7bb2","name":"Badrinath Temple","deity":"Vishnu (Badrinarayan)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Char Dham","Panch Badri","Chota Char Dham"],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Chamoli","town":"Badrinath","latitude":30.7433,"longitude":79.4938,"sandhya_friendly":"yes","sandhya_notes":"Tapt Kund, a hot-spring bathing ghat, sits right below the temple steps on the Alaknanda.","samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Annadanam schemes (including Badari-BAKASS) running year-round, supplemented by devotee-run bhandaras in season","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.3,"nearest_river_name":"Alaknanda","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Open only ~May to early Nov; closed and snowbound the rest of the year.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T20:00:08.393447+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition relates that Vishnu performed penance here while Lakshmi sheltered him from the Himalayan cold as a badari (jujube) tree, giving the place its name. The shrine is closed through the winter, when the deity is worshipped at Joshimath. Also called Vishal Badri, this is the principal shrine of the Panch Badri circuit, alongside Yogadhyan, Bhavishya, Vridha, and Adi Badri.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"बद्रीनाथ मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,