well when their spade struck a buried idol, drawing blood, and the well immediately filled with water despite the area's drought. Devotees still travel to Kanipakam to swear oaths of truth beside this temple tank, an unusual practice believed to continue an old local custom of settling disputes here.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"శ్రీ వరసిద్ధి వినాయక స్వామి దేవస్థానం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tirupati Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":50.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chittoor","nearest_railway_distance_km":12,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"558361ca-1d5a-4d81-9941-defd60137f82","name":"Kamaksha Temple","deity":"Kamaksha Devi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Mandi","town":"Jai Devi","latitude":31.50061,"longitude":76.95657,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kansa Khola River","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A historic mountain-ringed temple at Jaidevi in Mandi district, regarded as the family deity of the Suket royal house and the presiding goddess of the old Suket state. Kamaksha is understood as the goddess who fulfils desires. Other deities honoured at the site include Mahunag Ji and Bala Tika Ji Kafla Ji.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_clo