":null},{"id":"559958c7-6ea7-4854-9ff4-31d6bb24bca0","name":"Kailasanathar Temple, Murappanadu","deity":"Kailasanathar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Nava Kailasam"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tirunelveli","town":"Murappanadu","latitude":8.7247,"longitude":77.8319,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Thamirabarani","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T19:44:35.569161+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"The fifth of the Nava Kailasam, traditionally said to have been built by a Vallala king. A local legend tells of a Chola king whose daughter was born with a horse's face, cured after bathing at this spot on Shiva's instruction. A folk tradition links this shrine to Guru (Jupiter) among the nine planets.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"கைலாசநாதர் கோயில், முறப்பநாடு","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":21.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Seydunganallur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition (Agastya-Romasa Muni legend)","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"55ead3f9-e780-4391-9864-610b200ba498","name":"Maa Sharda Devi Temple, Maihar","deity":"Sharda Devi, regarded as an incarnation of Saraswati","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":["Shakti Peetha"],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Maihar","town":"Maihar","latitude":24.2612,"longitude":80.72316,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Navratri (both Chaitra and Sharad) is the major festival, with nine days of cultural performances.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:07:42.20596+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-22T09:07:42.20596+00:00","sthala_purana":"Shakti Peetha legend holds that Sati's necklace (har) fell here after Shiva carried her body, giving Maihar (Mai + har) its name — presented as legend, not history. Temple tradition dates the structure to around 502 CE, but that early date rests on tradition rather than archaeological verification, so it isn't asserted here as settled fact. Local legend also credits the warrior brothers Alha and Udal, of the Alha-Khand epic, as the temple's first devotees — Alha is said to have attained immortality through twelve years of penance here, again folklore rather than documented history.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Ropeway timings run roughly 6:30am–7:30pm, varying with season, weather and the sandhya aarti — approximate, not an official published schedule.","accessibility_notes":"1,064 steps lead to the hilltop shrine on Trikuta Hill; a ropeway (operated by Damodar Ropeways & Infra Ltd) is available for those unable to climb. Wheelchair access is very limited.","nearest_airport_name":"Khajuraho Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":148,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Maihar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Shakti Peetha tradition; Alha-Khand epic (folklore); temple tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"56107ae8-8ccf-441e-9f4e-f5d42e1b20d3","name":"Bagalamukhi Temple, Nalkheda","deity":"Bagalamukhi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Agar Malwa","town":"Gudrawan","latitude":23.84157,"longitude":76.23375,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Lakhundar River","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:13:52.370722+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Hindu temple at Nalkheda in Agar Malwa district, Madhya Pradesh, on the banks of the Lakhundar River, a tributary of the Narmada. It is dedicated to Bagalamukhi, one of the ten Tantric Mahavidya goddesses, who is associated with the colour yellow.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Raja Bhoj Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":127.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sarangpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":38.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bagalamukhi Temple, Nalkheda), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"561cc77b-8083-4aea-8c00-5189d8b1f61d","name":"Kanaka Durga Temple, Vijayawada","deity":"Kanaka Durga","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"NTR","town":"Vijayawada","latitude":16.5081,"longitude":80.6122,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Temple Anna Prasadam — free unlimited meals through the day","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0.1,"nearest_river_name":"Krishna","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb, especially Dasara/Sharannavaratri when the hill is illuminated; Vijayawada sits on the Andhra coast, where cyclone risk peaks in Oct–Nov ahead of the cooler, drier stretch that follows.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Sited on the Indrakeeladri hill above the Krishna river. Tradition holds that Arjuna performed penance on this hill to obtain the Pashupatastra from Shiva, and that the Devi installed herself here afterward as Kanaka Durga.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"కనక దుర్గ ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Vijayawada Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":20.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vijayawada Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"56884f0c-f576-43e2-8402-48bc0c913824","name":"Govind Dev Ji Temple","deity":"Radha and Krishna as Govind Dev","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Jaipur","town":"Jaipur","latitude":26.92883,"longitude":75.82395,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Amanisha River","river_distance_km":2.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:36.374917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A major Radha Krishna temple inside the City Palace complex in Jaipur, founded in the 18th century by Maharaja Jai Singh II, who brought the deities from Vrindavan. The Govind Dev image is counted among the seven principal Goswami deities of Vrindavan and, by tradition, is linked with Rupa Goswami.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jaipur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":11.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Jaipur Junction railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Govind Dev Ji Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"56d0818a-5bed-49f2-9c27-b099974754f3","name":"Charaut Math","deity":"Lakshminarayan","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Sitamarhi","town":"Choraut","latitude":26.531,"longitude":85.7936,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bighi Nadi River","river_distance_km":6.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:36.374917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old temple at Charaut in Sitamarhi, Bihar, belonging to the Lakshminarayan monastic order in the Mithila region. Its age is suggested by its copper vessels, heavy brass bells and brass and silver doors. It was also an important centre of Sanskrit and Vedic learning in Mithila.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Darbhanga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":39.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Janakpur Road railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Charaut Math), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"56d2e55b-7bfa-4f61-b546-12361374eaaa","name":"Kalugasalamoorthy temple","deity":"Murugan as Kalugasalamoorthy","sampradaya":"Kaumara","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Thoothukudi","town":"Kazhugumalai","latitude":9.14944,"longitude":77.70306,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Nichabanadhi River","river_distance_km":12.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:14.599574+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Murugan temple at Kalugumalai in Thoothukudi district, with a rock-cut core in early Pandyan style and Dravidian features. It is believed to have been expanded in the 18th century. Major festivals include Vaikasi Visagam, Kanthasasti, Thaipoosam and Panguni Uthiram.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Open 5:30 am to 12:30 pm and 4:30 pm to 9 pm.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":59,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kumarapuram railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":15,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kalugasalamoorthy temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Dravidian; rock-cut","construction_century":18},{"id":"56f21738-335c-4898-8312-912807835807","name":"Yathothkari Perumal Temple, Kanchipuram","deity":"Yathothkari Perumal (Vishnu) / Komalavalli","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Kanchipuram","town":"Kanchipuram","latitude":12.82417,"longitude":79.71222,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vegavathy","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-09T13:54:39.898029+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Also called the Tiruvekkaa Temple and locally known as Sonnavannam Seitha Perumal, one of the 108 Divya Desams and the second-largest temple in southern Kanchipuram after the Varadaraja Perumal Temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Chennai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":52.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kanchipuram East railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Nalayira Divya Prabandham; local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian, Pallava origins","construction_century":null},{"id":"572c6a43-f0a9-49ae-80f0-f5b0cef5be61","name":"Ajgaibinath Temple, Sultanganj","deity":"Shiva, as a swayambhu (self-manifested) linga continuously bathed by the Ganga","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Kanwar pilgrimage"],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Bhagalpur","town":"Sultanganj","latitude":25.2524,"longitude":86.7343,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganga","river_distance_km":0,"best_season_notes":"The Shravani Mela during Sawan (the monsoon month) is central here — Kanwariyas collect Ganga water at this spot, traditionally called Uttar Vahini Ganga, as the starting point of the roughly 105km walk to Baidyanath Dham, Deoghar (some continue on to Basukinath, already in this database, which names Ajgaibinath as one of the region's three major Shiva temples).","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:21:41.744062+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition, set in the Treta Yuga, holds that Rama worshipped Shiva here before the battle with Ravana — legend, not verifiable history. The shrine sits on a rocky island in the Ganges, shaped like a boat; its current Nagara-style shikhara was rebuilt and donated in 1885 by Rani Kalavati of the local royal family, which is the documented architectural date.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":"Reaching the island shrine requires a boat or ferry crossing, typically from Murli Hills, Sultanganj.","nearest_airport_name":"Purnea Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":88.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sultanganj railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local tradition (Treta Yuga legend); 1885 donation records","architecture_style":"Rock-built Nagara-style shrine on a river-island rock outcrop, shaped like a boat","construction_century":19},{"id":"57c4e513-4815-4a8e-9060-e00a38535311","name":"Yaganti Uma Maheshwara Temple","deity":"Uma Maheshwara (Shiva-Parvati)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Kurnool","town":"Yaganti","latitude":15.1667,"longitude":78.2833,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kundu River","river_distance_km":7.6,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; Shivaratri is the busiest day.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Believed to date to around the 5th–6th centuries, with later additions credited to the Vijayanagara period. The temple is best known for its Nandi statue in the sanctum, whose stone is documented to slowly enlarge over time — by tradition, the 16th-century saint Potuluri Veera Brahmendra Swamy prophesied it would keep growing until it fills the shrine at the end of the Kali Yuga, at which point it will come alive.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"యాగంటి ఉమామహేశ్వర ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Uyyalawada Narasimha Reddy Airport ,   Kurnool","nearest_airport_distance_km":62.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Sanjamala railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"57c51c19-a0a9-46cf-ac37-a721bbe1a95c","name":"Veerabhadra Temple, Lepakshi","deity":"Veerabhadra (fierce form of Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":["Vijayanagara monument"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Sri Sathya Sai","town":"Lepakshi","latitude":13.8047,"longitude":77.6081,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kushavati River","river_distance_km":12.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:23:03.123234+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in the 1530s under the Vijayanagara Empire by brothers Viranna and Virupanna, governors under Achyuta Deva Raya, the temple is renowned for its \"hanging pillar\" — one of around 70 carved granite pillars whose base does not touch the floor — and for a giant monolithic Nandi carved from a single boulder nearby, along with an unfinished Kalyana Mandapam and the largest single-stone Naga-linga in India, a multi-hooded serpent sheltering a Shiva linga. Local tradition ties the town's name to the Ramayana: Rama is said to have found the vulture-king Jatayu here, mortally wounded after trying to stop Ravana's abduction of Sita, and to have addressed him as \"Le Pakshi\" (Telugu, roughly \"rise, bird\").","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"వీరభద్ర స్వామి దేవాలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sri Sathya Sai Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":43.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Hindupur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition; ASI documentation","architecture_style":"Vijayanagara","construction_century":16},{"id":"57c9aee4-5539-4d4a-a6aa-78eb8dc41ac6","name":"Chaubara Dera No. 1","deity":"Shiva (probable, based on Shaivite imagery)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Khargone","town":"Khargone Tahsil","latitude":21.82171,"longitude":75.45458,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kunda River","river_distance_km":14.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:36.374917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The largest of a cluster of ruined temples in the village of Un, Madhya Pradesh. Its original name is lost, its spire is wholly destroyed and the main image in the sanctum is missing. Because of the amount of Shaivite imagery, it is thought to have been a Shiva temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Jalgaon Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":97.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":null,"nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Chaubara Dera No. 1), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"5914024a-6159-4656-9204-48d42a40ec78","name":"Gundicha Temple, Puri","deity":"Jagannath, with Balabhadra and Subhadra (present only during Rath Yatra — the temple is unoccupied the rest of the year)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Rath Yatra"],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Puri","town":"Puri","latitude":19.81692,"longitude":85.84036,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dhaudia River","river_distance_km":3.2,"best_season_notes":"This is the temple of the Rath Yatra itself (usually Jun–Jul, per the Odia lunar calendar), when the three deities are pulled here from the main Jagannath Temple in massive chariots and stay for seven days before returning via the Bahuda Yatra. Sub-festivals during the stay include Hera Panchami (5th day) and Dakshina Moda (6th day).","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:41:30.569832+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Temple legend attributes the founding to King Indradyumna, the legendary founder of the main Jagannath Temple, naming it for his queen Gundicha — presented here as sthala purana, not independently verified history. The building itself is dated by scholars to the 12th century CE, built under the Eastern Ganga king Anantavarman Chodaganga Deva (whose reign, roughly 1078–1150 CE, also produced the main Jagannath Temple). Each year the three deities travel here in their chariots and are installed for a week, in what's popularly called Lord Jagannath's \"Garden House\" or, less formally, his aunt's house.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":48.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Puri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Temple tradition (Indradyumna legend); Eastern Ganga dynasty records","architecture_style":"Kalinga Deula, pidha (pyramidal-roof) style; grey sandstone ashlar masonry with iron dowels","construction_century":12},{"id":"5932113a-ccc3-4b9e-baa3-110ce8b3c2c1","name":"Somarama","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh",