m a tank first created by Adi Shankaracharya in the 8th century. Tradition holds the rivers Narmada and Son, born here together, were betrothed to marry but Son abandoned Narmada at the altar — she flows west to the Arabian Sea in anger and disappointment, while Son flows east to join the Ganges.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"नर्मदा उद्गम मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Bilasa Devi Kevat Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":84.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhanwar Tonk railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":16.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":11},{"id":"59cef5aa-a79e-4ec3-afb5-81d999409dc1","name":"Nandi Temple, Khajuraho","deity":"Nandi, the mount of Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Chhatarpur","town":"Khajuraho","latitude":24.85331,"longitude":79.92269,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khudar River","river_distance_km":1.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A small temple at Khajuraho housing Nandi, the bull who carries Shiva. In keeping with the usual pattern of a seated Nandi facing the main deity, it stands opposite the Vishvanatha Temple of Shiva. It is one of the monuments in the Khajuraho Group, a World Heritage Site.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":nu