try":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Bankura","town":"Vishnupur","latitude":23.07111,"longitude":87.32417,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dwarakeshwar River","river_distance_km":3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:27.898205+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Krishna temple in the town of Bishnupur in Bankura district, West Bengal, also known as the Pancha-ratna temple. Krishna is worshipped here in the form of Shyam, and an image of Radha is worshipped alongside him.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":62.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bishnupur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shyam Ray Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Pancha-ratna (five-pinnacle)","construction_century":null},{"id":"5b42d3fe-bd5e-4f67-b8be-a8dc417c2dc8","name":"Vijayasana Perumal Temple, Natham","deity":"Vijayasana Perumal (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Nava Tirupati"],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Thoothukudi","town":"Natham","latitude":8.637056,"longitude":77.924139,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Thamirabarani","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T10:54:38.493897+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of the Nava Tirupati and a Divya Desam, also called Thiruvaragunamangai. Tradition holds a Brahmin named Vedhavi performed penance here chanting the \"Aasana mantra,\" and Vishnu — pleased with his devotion — appeared before him and granted him moksha; hence the deity is known as Vijayasana Perumal, with Lakshmi as Varagunavalli. Within the Nava Tirupati's parallel association with the nine planets, this shrine is linked to Chandra (the Moon).","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"விஜயாசன பெருமாள் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Srivaikuntam railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"5b542990-a1b8-4014-b5b6-eb4de38c853b","name":"Shri Katyayani Baneshwar Temple, Aversa","deity":"Katyayani","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Uttara Kannada","town":"Avarsa","latitude":14.72333,"longitude":74.27972,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gangavali River","river_distance_km":13.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:38.196668+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in the coastal town of Aversa near Ankola, Uttara Kannada. Katyayani is the family deity of many Konkani Gaud Saraswat Brahmins, Saraswat Brahmins, Daivajnya Brahmins and Konkani Kharvis. A trust manages the temple, and the complex runs on solar energy.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Goa International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":87.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Harwada railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Katyayani Baneshwar Temple, Aversa), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"5b7a003f-0edb-4bdf-8f8b-76c99801e1e7","name":"Krishna Janmasthan Temple Complex","deity":"Krishna","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Mathura","town":"Mathura","latitude":27.50475,"longitude":77.66975,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mathura Escape River","river_distance_km":0.9,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple complex in Mathura at the traditional birthplace of Krishna, with the Keshavdev temple, the Garbh Griha and Bhagvata Bhavan, where Radha Krishna are the presiding deities. The site is said to be sacred since at least the 6th century BCE. Earlier temples were destroyed several times, last in 1670, and the present complex was built in the 20th century.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_op