ort_distance_km":5.1,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Palavanthangal railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Contributor-submitted local survey","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"631f7f2e-a727-46e9-bdfe-4b466dce36fa","name":"Vaishno Devi Temple, Katra","deity":"Vaishno Devi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":"Reasi","town":"Katra","latitude":33.0306,"longitude":74.9496,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"pure_veg_available","food_source_name":"Shri Mata Vaishno Devi Shrine Board Bhojanalaya (along the trek route and at Bhawan)","food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":0,"nearest_river_name":"Chenab River","river_distance_km":12.5,"best_season_notes":"Mar–Oct is most comfortable for the ~13km uphill trek; winter brings snow and ice on the path.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition holds that Vaishno Devi, an incarnation of Adi Shakti, took human form as a devotee of Rama before withdrawing to these hills to meditate. Pursued by the tantric Bhairavnath, she is said to have fought and ultimately beheaded him at a cave further up the mountain (now Bhairon Ghati) before manifesting herself permanently as three natural rock formations (pindis) in the main cave, representing Mahakali, Mahalakshmi, and Mahasaraswati together.","etiquette_notes":"Reached only via a roughly 13km uphill trek (or palanquin/pony/helicopter services available for a fee) — plan footwear and pacing accordingly rather than treating it as a normal temple visit. Modest dress is expected; no strict Kerala-style dress code applies here.","native_name":"वैष्णो देवी मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"The Bhawan offers darshan 24 hours a day, closing only briefly for the Mangala Aarti (roughly 6:20–8am) and evening Aarti (roughly 7:20–8:30pm). Waiting time varies hugely by season, from 1–2 hours in Feb/Mar to 6–9 hours during festivals.","accessibility_notes":"Reached only via a roughly 13km uphill trek from the base camp at Katra. Options besides walking: pony, palanquin (palki, carried by porters), and a battery-operated vehicle for part of the route; a helicopter service covers most of the climb for a fee. Not accessible by wheelchair over the trek itself.","nearest_airport_name":"Jammu Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":48,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Katra Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2,"emergency_contact_notes":"Dial 112 for all-India emergency services. The Vaishno Devi Shrine Board maintains help desks, medical aid posts, and battery-car/pony rescue points along the whole Katra-Bhawan route.","sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition, not a single classical Sanskrit text","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"635f2d5f-61ce-4854-9420-00a2b1e61519","name":"Isanesvara Siva Temple","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar Municipal Corporation","latitude":20.25306,"longitude":85.84333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Dayaa River","river_distance_km":4.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A 13th-century temple in the old town of Bhubaneswar, dated from its architecture to the Ganga period. It faces east and stands in the Gosagaresvara precinct, close to the Lingaraja temple. The sanctum has only a circular yoni pitha because the linga is missing. It is still used for worship and for public meetings.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":3.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Isanesvara Siva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Kalinga, Ganga period","construction_century":13},{"id":"63dd4ffa-f554-4c17-aa77-7362b3f12d17","name":"Ahobila Narasimha Temple, Upper Ahobilam","deity":"Ahobila Narasimha (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Nava Narasimha"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Nandyal","town":"Ahobilam","latitude":15.135,"longitude":78.79,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bhavanasini","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; the forest trek to Upper Ahobilam is best avoided in peak summer or heavy monsoon.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T19:58:00.742097+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"The principal and most ancient of the Nava Narasimha, also called Ugra Narasimha — the fierce form in which Vishnu tore apart Hiranyakashipu. The sanctum is a low, naturally occurring cave in the hillside, with a swayambhu (self-manifested) image.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"అహోబిల నరసింహ ఆలయం","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kadapa Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":68.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Diguvametta railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":29.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition (Nava Narasimha Kshetra)","architecture_style":"Dravidian, carved into the hillside","construction_century":14},{"id":"63e2aa32-63d6-4b05-8b61-d66ee8c737be","name":"Raidongia Doul","deity":"Shiva (originally a Devi temple)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Assam","district":"Dibrugarh","town":"Dibrugarh West","latitude":27.2825,"longitude":94.7928,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Burhi Dihing River","river_distance_km":0.7,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A doul in the Lejai-Kalakhowa area of Dibrugarh district built in 1750 by the Ahom king Pramatta Singha. It began as a Devi temple, but over time local people took to worshipping Shiva here, so it is also called Shiv Doul. Maha Shivratri is the main festival, and the state protects the monument.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dibrugarh Mohanbari Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":31.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khowang railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":10.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Raidongia Doul), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Ahom","construction_century":18},{"id":"6444eab8-b958-40d1-bc89-9fd4060532f3","name":"Aundha Nagnath Temple","deity":"Shiva as Nagnath (Jyotirlinga)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Hingoli","town":"Wagarwadi","latitude":19.53709,"longitude":77.04151,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Purna River","river_distance_km":7.6,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Shiva temple in Hingoli district, regarded as the eighth of the twelve Jyotirlingas. It blends Hemadpanti and Maratha styles and has a distinctive basement sanctum. A legend tells of the temple turning for the saint Namdev. A chariot festival takes place at Mahashivratri, and the ASI protects it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shri Guru Gobind Singh Ji Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":49.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chondi railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":16.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Aundha Nagnath Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Hemadpanti and Maratha","construction_century":null},{"id":"646b2710-a55a-47f9-aa3d-5797fe73d378","name":"Duladeo Temple","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Chhatarpur","town":"Khajuraho","latitude":24.85306,"longitude":79.91944,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khudar River","river_distance_km":2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Chandela-period Shiva temple at Khajuraho with a linga in the sanctum, dated to 1000-1150 CE and counted as the last of the Chandela temples. It follows a seven-chariot plan, has softly expressive sculpture and celestial dancers, and is part of the UNESCO-listed Khajuraho group.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Khajuraho Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":4.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khajuraho railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Duladeo Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Chandela, saptaratha plan","construction_century":11},{"id":"6489c645-5dda-461d-800a-6126f2b66d29","name":"Ranganathaswamy Temple, Srirangapatna","deity":"Ranganatha (Adi Ranga)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Pancharanga Kshetram"],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Mandya","town":"Srirangapatna","latitude":12.424722,"longitude":76.679722,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kaveri","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-05T10:54:38.493897+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"The first of the five Pancharanga Kshetrams — temples to Ranganatha (a form of Vishnu) strung along the Kaveri river — earning this shrine the name Adi Ranga, \"the first Ranga,\" counting downstream toward Srirangam. Built in 984 CE by Tirumalaiah, a local chief under the Western Ganga dynasty, on the site of an older shrine; in the 12th century the Hoysala king Vishnuvardhana granted the surrounding village to the philosopher-saint Ramanujacharya.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ಶ್ರೀ ರಂಗನಾಥಸ್ವಾಮಿ ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನ","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Mysore Mandakalli Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":21.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Shrirangapattana railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":"Dravidian (Western Ganga / Hoysala)","construction_century":10},{"id":"65280733-d05a-4c21-8ef2-46f5b43fe5fa","name":"Avittathur Mahadeva Temple","deity":"Shiva as Mahadeva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Thrissur","town":"Avittathur","latitude":10.33489,"longitude":76.24535,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kurumali River","river_distance_km":8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An ancient Shiva temple in Avittathur village, Thrissur district, Kerala, a village counted among the 64 original Brahmin settlements of Kerala. It is said to be over 2000 years old, and four old inscriptions have been found. Folklore credits the sage Agastya with installing the image, while another belief names Parasurama; it is one of the 108 Shiva temples of Kerala.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":26.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Irinjalakuda railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.9,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Avittathur Mahadeva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"6553fbe6-ec5f-449a-a0c9-a391b8575951","name":"Shitala Mata Mandir, Sandila","deity":"Shitala","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttar Pradesh","district":"Hardoi","town":"Sandila","latitude":27.07117,"longitude":80.50484,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:27.898205+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:35.665826+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old temple of the goddess Shitala in Sandila, Uttar Pradesh. According to tradition, the Vedic sage Shandilya performed penance here, and the site is therefore also called Shandilya Rishi Tapobhumi.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"acces